ountry></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIHARA SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASAMA NOBUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUOKA YASUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIWA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OUMI MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHIBA, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIHARA, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAMA, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUOKA, YASUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIWA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OUMI, MANABU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A near-field optical head (3000) which can be produced using a silicon process and can permit the irradiation and detection of light through a fine aperture while being positioned stably close to media, and which comprises a fine aperture (3008) formed at the apex of a taper, a light introduction unit (3002) for allowing light to propagate in approximately parallel to media, and a light reflection layer (3001) for reflecting the light propagated through the light introduction unit (3002) in the direction of the fine aperture (3008), the head is further provided with a condensing function capable of irradiating light condensed on the fine aperture (3008).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, il est possible de produire une tête optique à champ proche (3000) au moyen d'un procédé au silicium; cette tête permet le rayonnement et la détection de la lumière à travers une mince ouverture, tout en étant positionnée de manière stable à proximité d'un support, et elle comprend une mince ouverture (3008) formée au niveau du sommet d'un cône, une unité d'introduction de lumière (3002), permettant la propagation de la lumière de manière approximativement parallèle au support, ainsi qu'une couche de réflexion (3001) de lumière, destinée à réfléchir la lumière propagée à travers l'unité d'introduction (3002), en direction de l'ouverture (3008). En outre, cette tête est dotée d'une fonction de condensation permettant le rayonnement de la lumière condensée sur l'ouverture (3008).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>